// cp Debug.example.xcconfig Debug.local.xcconfig
//
// Gitignored, and included by Debug.xcconfig if it exists. This is where a
// machine-specific endpoint goes, so nobody has to edit a committed file to
// point at their own laptop — and so nobody accidentally commits it when they
// do.
//
// Only override what you need; anything left out keeps the Debug default.

// --- Physical device -----------------------------------------------------
// The Simulator's localhost is the Mac running it, so the default just works
// there. A real iPhone needs a host it can reach, and it has to be **https**:
// the app carries no ATS exception, so plain HTTP to a LAN address is blocked
// (project.yml says why that is deliberate).
//
// Easiest is a tunnel in front of `make dev` — Tailscale serves a valid cert
// for a machine name, and `ngrok http 8080` prints one per run.
//
// API_SCHEME = https
// API_HOSTNAME = your-mac.tailnet-name.ts.net

// --- A deployed backend ---------------------------------------------------
// Running the Debug app against Railway — useful for reproducing something that
// only happens against real data, without archiving a Release build.
//
// API_SCHEME = https
// API_HOSTNAME = api-production-22b5.up.railway.app
